      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Functionality / Security (Integer Overflow):** `offset + bytes` can overflow if `bytes` is very large (e.g., when a caller passes a negative `int size`). If it wraps around to a value smaller than `CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE_BYTES`, this out-of-bounds check is bypassed, potentially returning `EC_SUCCESS` for an invalid write.\n\nSuggestion:\n```c\n\t/* Invalid value */\n\tif (bytes \u003e CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE_BYTES || offset \u003e CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE_BYTES - bytes) {\n\t\treturn EC_ERROR_INVAL;\n\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/2db4616b-922f-4478-98e7-dbe7e3c5b67e)",
