      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Architecture / Error Handling:** If `spi_flash_reg_to_protect` fails (e.g., due to an undecodable status), it returns an error code here. However, the callers currently discard this specific return value and hardcode `EC_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED`.\n\nIt is cleaner to explicitly map undecodable statuses to `EC_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED` here (fulfilling the fail-closed policy) and then let callers propagate the returned error code. This ensures `EC_ERROR_INVAL` from the bounds check above isn\u0027t incorrectly masked as `EC_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED`.\n\nSuggestion:\n```c\n\trv \u003d spi_flash_reg_to_protect(sr1, sr2, \u0026start, \u0026len);\n\n\tif (rv) {\n\t\t/* Fail closed on undecodable status */\n\t\treturn EC_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED;\n\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/2db4616b-922f-4478-98e7-dbe7e3c5b67e)",
